    "sha": "18d9ab15e5d4178627e29e83d06180c25502764c",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDE4ZDlhYjE1ZTVkNDE3ODYyN2UyOWU4M2QwNjE4MGMyNTUwMjc2NGM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T14:53:03Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T14:53:03Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(mcp): list every accepted field of a kind in list_operation_types\n\nlist_operation_types named only the fields that the default params\nserialize. Optional fields (pocket tilt and rest, the plasma feed and\npierce keys, the Wire Contour extras) and the words of an enum field\nwere not listed.\n\nA serde shape trace of ParamsDto (mcp/kind_fields/trace.rs) now drives\nthe DTO's own Deserialize and records the struct fields, the enum\nvariants and the Option fields of each kind. A field absent from the\ndefaults gets \"optional\": true, an enum field gets \"values\", and an\nobject or array field gets a short \"shape\" text. The two kinds that\nflatten a struct (thread, sinker_side_burn) trace the flattened type by\nitself. A kind that cannot be traced gets \"fields_incomplete\": true.\n\nFixes #3449\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
